{"id": "q0051", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2702078363, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "Gary bought a boat for $9000.  Over the first year it depreciated 30%.  The second year it depreciated another 30%.  The third year it depreciated 20%.  How much is the boat worth after the three years?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0051.wav", "input_sha256": "ed2b21ccc3a8461b463e87de9cc78c3e895033650ae31f50c1477c319fb7f2ec", "input_samples": 274800, "input_s": 17.175, "n_real_chunks": 18, "score": 0.197, "act": 0.9985, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So Gary bought a boat for $9, 000. In the first year it depreci ated 30%, so that means it lost 2 700 dollars in value. So after the first year it' s worth 6, 30 0 dollars. The second year it de preciated another 3 0%, so that means it lost another 1, 89 0 dollars in value. So after the second year it's worth 4, 4 1 0 dollars. The third year it depreciated 20%, so that means it lost another 8 8 2 dollars in value. So after the third year it' s worth 3,5 28 dollars. So the answer is 3, 5 28.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 17, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 47, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0051_local_local.wav", "sha256": "983b547fc5993ca4adbb24eff2910acc5ae8794ed783e23e2fbc1fa4ac0e2d6d", "sr": 24000, "seconds