{"id": "q0075", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2488653568, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "Jake is shopping at a clothing store. The store has a buy one get one 50% off deal on T-shirts. Jake buys 2 T-shirts. The original price of each T-shirt is $8. Then, Jake buys a pair of shoes that is 40% off the original price. The original price of the shoes is $40. What is the total amount of money Jake spends at the store?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0075.wav", "input_sha256": "718c9f89dcc1b4e187100e0c799efedf8266ac17af8f537da6046267348e8a40", "input_samples": 401600, "input_s": 25.1, "n_real_chunks": 26, "score": 0.2491, "act": 0.9996, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Jake buys two t-shirts at a buy one get one 50% off deal. Each t- shirt is $8. So the first t-shirt he pays full price for, which is $8. The second one gets 5 0% off, so that's half of $8, which is $4. Add ing those together, $8 plus $4 gives him $12 for the t-shirts.Then he buy s shoes that are 40% off the original price of $40. First, find the discount amount: 40% of $40 is 0.4 times 4 0, which equal s $16. So the sale price of the shoes is $ 40 minus $ 16, which is $24. Now add the cost of the t-shirts and the shoes: $1 2 plus $2 4 equal s $36. Therefore, the total amount of money Jake spends at the store is 36.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 25, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak