{"id": "q0097", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3839400866, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "Mark's car breaks down and he needs to get a new radiator.  The cost for a new radiator is $400 but he goes to get it at a junk shop and gets it for 80% off.  He then hires a mechanic to install it and it takes 3 hours at $50 an hour.  How much did he pay?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0097.wav", "input_sha256": "45f43b7c397a695e39ba151b7ea0f7ae6a02665a18d449d0a28dcc09674722ed", "input_samples": 332200, "input_s": 20.762, "n_real_chunks": 21, "score": 0.1448, "act": 0.9994, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The cost of the ra diator was $40 0, but he got it for 80% off. So first, let's calculate how much he paid for the radiator. 2 0% of $ 400 is equal to $80. That means he paid $8 0 for the ra diator.Then, the mechanic charged him $5 0 an hour for 3 hours of work. So, that would be $ 1 5 0 for the installation. Add ing the two amounts together, we get $ 80 plus $1 50, which equal s $2 30. Therefore, Mark paid a total of $2 30.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 20, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 38, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0097_local_local.wav", "sha256": "266f307f236f6e20624532d368d00e1fdecaa0c12cbccf512d527d22aabddd74", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 38.28}}, 