{"id": "q0242", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 580437262, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "The lowest point on Earth is the bottom of the Mariana Trench at a depth of 35,840 feet below sea level. The highest point on Earth is the summit of Mt. Everest at a height of 29,028 feet above sea level. Which of the following is the best estimate of the distance between the lowest and highest points on Earth?\n\nA. 75,000 feet\nB. 65,000 feet\nC. 55,000 feet\nD. 60,000 feet\nE. 7,000 feet\nF. 64,000 feet\nG. 70,000 feet\nH. 50,000 feet\nI. 6,000 feet\nJ. 80,000 feet\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0242.wav", "input_sha256": "4e7d28604264753fb9e1a4de2796558a79cb54b5e50911b3dfb049871f86ce90", "input_samples": 677800, "input_s": 42.362, "n_real_chunks": 43, "score": 0.1446, "act": 0.9988, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So let's figure out the total distance between the bottom of the Mariana Trench and the top of Mount Everest. The trench is 35, 8 4 5 feet below sea level, and Mount Ever est is 29, 02 8 feet above sea level. To find the total distance, we add those two numbers together because one is below and one is above. So 35, 8 45 plus 29, 02 8 equal s about 6 4,8 7 3 feet. That puts us closest to option F, which is 64, 000 feet.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 38, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 34, "feed_lag_max_ms": 330, "feed_lag_sum_m