{"id": "q0256", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1022242902, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "A voltage source 60cos1000t V is in series with a 2-k\\Omega resistor and a 1 -\\muFcapacitor. Findi_forced.\n\nA. i_forced= 28cos1000t - 14 sin 1000tmA\nB. i_forced= 24cos1000t - 12 sin 1000tmA\nC. i_forced= 20cos1000t + 10 sin 1000tmA\nD. i_forced= 30cos1000t - 15 sin 1000tmA\nE. i_forced= 15cos1000t - 30 sin 1000tmA\nF. i_forced= 30cos1000t + 15 sin 1000tmA\nG. i_forced= 24cos1000t + 12 sin 1000tmA\nH. i_forced= 20cos1000t - 10 sin 1000tmA\nI. i_forced= 26cos1000t - 13 sin 1000tmA\nJ. i_forced= 28cos1000t + 14 sin 1000tmA\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0256.wav", "input_sha256": "8c596153634fd58d86c598ed0cd024f00557731ee61ae5c74c3d7106e641cf58", "input_samples": 942600, "input_s": 58.913, "n_real_chunks": 59, "score": 0.8043, "act": 0.9986, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Let's find the forced current i_f. We have a 6 0 cos1 000t V source in series with a 2 kΩ resistor and a 1 μF capacitor. First, convert everything to s-domain. The voltage source becomes V_s = 60 cos100 0t, so its phasor is 6 0 angle 0°. The imped ance of the resistor is just R = 2000 oh ms. For the capacitor, Z C = 1/ jω C. W av es are at 1000 rad/s, and C is 1 microfar ad, so ZC = 1/ j * 1 000 * 1e- 6 = -j 1000 ohms. Now total impedance Z_ total = R + ZC = 2 000 - j 1000 oh ms. To find the current, use Ohm' s law: I_f = V_s / Z_total. Substit ute: I_f = 60 angle 0° / [ 2 000 - j 100 0]. Convert the denominator to polar form. Magn", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_